Binary Search
--------------

Binary Search is a technique used to reduce the search space by half repeatedly.
Instead of checking every element one by one:

Compare with the middle
Decide whether the answer lies on the left or right
Continue on that half

Time Complexity:

Binary Search → O(log n)
Linear Search → O(n)


1. Basic Binary Search : Used on a sorted array.

        If target < middle → go left
        If target > middle → go right

        Formula:   mid = low + (high - low) / 2

        This avoids integer overflow.

Patterns:
        | Pattern             | Concept                 |
        | ------------------- | ----------------------- |
      1  | Exact Search        | Find target             |
      2  | Lower Bound         | First >= target         |
      3  | Upper Bound         | First > target          |
      4 | First Occurrence    | Leftmost target         |
      5  | Last Occurrence     | Rightmost target        |
      6  | Search Answer Space | Binary search on answer |
      7   | Rotated Array       | Modified binary search  |
      8  | Peak Problems       | Binary search on trend  |
      9 | Infinite Array      | Expand + binary search  |
